# React + Vite Frontend Security

## Auth tokens
- Never `localStorage` for JWT — `httpOnly` cookies or in-memory.
- Auth state in a Redux slice; the axios interceptor reads from it. Nothing else.
- Refresh-token flow once in `packages/api-client`, never per feature.

## API calls
- Never interpolate user input into URL paths — parameterised route helpers.
- zod-validate user-supplied data before sending.
- No API keys in frontend. `VITE_` for non-secret config; secrets via server-side proxy.

## XSS
- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without DOMPurify.
- No `eval()` / `new Function()` with user-supplied strings.
- No template-string SQL/HTML construction in shared utilities.

## CSRF
- Cookie auth: `SameSite=Lax`/`Strict` + `Secure`.
- Double-submit token or `credentials: "include"` + CSRF header.
- WebSocket auth via URL/first-message, never cookies.

## Env vars
- All browser-exposed env vars prefixed `VITE_`. Document in `.env.example`.
- Never commit `.env` / `.env.local`. Secrets never in `VITE_`.
- Validate presence at startup; throw on missing critical vars.

## Dependency hygiene
- Pin majors. `pnpm audit` in CI; fail on high+. Lockfile committed.
- Review postinstall scripts on additions.

## CSP
- Strict CSP in production: `default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' wss://<host>`.
- No `unsafe-inline`. vanilla-extract emits static CSS — strict-style compatible.
- Report violations to a dedicated endpoint during rollout.
